        "“In the card” is wrong, because the money goes *on* a card, not inside it. “Pourboire” is French, so the English word *tip* is needed. “Make the tip with the card” and “tip by the card” are word-for-word French, and the last one is too formal.",
        "So: *Can I add the tip on the card?* Tip: add the tip on the card; give a cash tip in your hand."
